# Domains to SPLICE (pass through without decryption) instead of bumping.
# Use for certificate-pinned hosts that fail when SSL-bumped.
# One domain per line; a leading dot matches subdomains.
#
# Firefox pins certificates for its own Mozilla service connections, so bumping
# them causes errors — splice them through untouched.
.mozilla.org
.mozilla.com
.mozilla.net
.firefox.com
# Google: session-cookie binding (RotateCookies) breaks under SSL-bump, logging
# you out on every relaunch. Splice so TLS goes end-to-end. No cache loss — this
# traffic is no-store anyway. Static assets on gstatic.com/ytimg.com stay bumped.
.google.com
.youtube.com
.googleusercontent.com

# ===========================================================================
# Anti-bot / cert-pinned domains. Splicing restores the client's genuine TLS
# handshake end-to-end, so the origin sees a real browser JA3/JA4 + HTTP/2
# instead of Squid's OpenSSL fingerprint over HTTP/1.1 (the mismatch that
# bot-detection systems flag).
#
# Cost of splicing: that traffic becomes opaque (TCP_TUNNEL) and UNCACHEABLE.
# Keep this list tight — every entry added is cache value given up. Most of
# these serve no-store dynamic content anyway, so little is actually lost.
# ===========================================================================

# --- CAPTCHA / bot-detection infrastructure --------------------------------
# These actively fingerprint TLS; bumping them makes challenges unsolvable
# (endless CAPTCHA loops). Splice so the widget sees the real browser.
.hcaptcha.com
.recaptcha.net
.arkoselabs.com
.funcaptcha.com
.datadome.co
.perimeterx.net
.px-cloud.net
challenges.cloudflare.com

# --- Identity / SSO / MFA ---------------------------------------------------
# Session tokens are bound to the TLS channel; bumping logs you out or breaks
# the MFA handshake. (M365 is the classic case noted in CLAUDE.md.)
.microsoftonline.com
.office.com
.office365.com
.sharepoint.com
.live.com
.okta.com
.auth0.com
.duosecurity.com
.apple.com
.icloud.com

# --- Financial --------------------------------------------------------------
# Cert-pinned, and you almost certainly do not want to MITM your own banking:
# a bumped session is decryptable by whoever holds ca.key.
.paypal.com
.stripe.com

# Korean banking/fintech — included on the assumption this is your region.
# Delete freely if not relevant.
.kbstar.com
.shinhan.com
.wooribank.com
.hanabank.com
.nonghyup.com
.kakaobank.com
.tossbank.com
.toss.im
.kftc.or.kr

# --- Messaging (certificate pinning in native apps) -------------------------
.whatsapp.com
.whatsapp.net
.signal.org
.slack.com
.discord.com
.telegram.org
.kakao.com

# --- DRM / streaming --------------------------------------------------------
# Widevine/FairPlay license exchange fails under interception. Video segment
# CDNs are left bumped where possible so large objects still cache.
.netflix.com
.spotify.com
.disneyplus.com

# --- Aggressive bot management (ticketing / retail) -------------------------
.ticketmaster.com
.nike.com

